From 385de0891fc1e943db077be1321b702dc0941f4d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: impl <impl@invalid>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 02:34:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] sdk: C versions of small hw/lock/FIFO asm functions
 (SDK_PORT_3DS)

Eight HGSS NitroSDK files hold MWCC asm that GCC cannot compile. Each
function gets a C version under #ifdef SDK_PORT_3DS. The asm stays
unchanged under #else, so the DS build compiles the same text. The patch
only adds lines. Cross-checked against Platinum patch series 0006, 0015
and 0024 (see below).

Per function (line numbers in the pinned tree):

- OsCountZeroBits, os/os_vram_exclusive_clz.c:9-12. clz r0, r0 gives the
  count of leading zero bits, 32 for 0. C returns 32 for 0, because
  __builtin_clz(0) is undefined.
- OSi_WaitVCount0, os/os_init.c:3-14. Saves IME (32-bit ldr), stores
  HW_REG_BASE to IME (str r12), spins while VCOUNT (16-bit ldrh) is not 0,
  then restores the saved IME word. C uses the same accesses and widths.
- OS_Halt, os/os_terminate_proc.c:4-9 (ARM9 only). mcr p15, 0, r0, c7,
  c0, 4 is wait-for-interrupt. C calls NitroPort_Halt, which runs a frame
  and takes V-blank, so OS_Halt returns as the DS does after an interrupt.
- VENEER_SVC_WaitByLoop, os/os_spin_lock_id.c:34-37 (ARM7 only). A tail
  call to SVC_WaitByLoop.
- OS_UnLockCartridge and OS_UnLockCard, os/os_spin_lock_id.c:50-53 and
  60-63. Tail calls to OS_UnlockCartridge and OS_UnlockCard with the same
  argument.
- OS_GetLockID, os/os_spin_lock_id.c:71-121. Two words of free-ID bits:
  the first starts at OSi_ANYP_LOCK_ID_START, the second 32 IDs later. It
  takes the highest set bit (clz) of the first non-empty word, clears it,
  and returns base + clz. It returns OS_LOCK_ID_ERROR (-3) when both words
  are empty. C matches; clz is only called on a non-zero word.
- OS_ReleaseLockID, os/os_spin_lock_id.c:125-137. IDs from START + 32 up
  use the second word. It sets bit (0x80000000 >> offset). The ARM takes
  the shift count from the bottom byte of the offset, and a count of 32 or
  more gives 0, so nothing is freed. C takes the same byte, so the shift is
  always below 32 (no undefined shift on 64-bit hosts).
- GX_SendFifo48B and GX_SendFifo64B, gx/gxasm.c:10-20 and 24-32. They read
  12 or 16 words from pSrc in order (ldmia r0!). They store them with stmia
  r1 (no writeback) in groups of 3 or 8, so word i goes to pDest + 4 *
  (i % 3) or pDest + 4 * (i % 8). C stores each word to that address, in
  the same order.
- GXi_NopClearFifo128_, gx/g3x_nop_clear_fifo.c:9-47. 128 zero words in
  groups of four (stmia r0, no writeback). Word i goes to reg + 4 * (i % 4).
- RtcWaitBusy, rtc/rtc_api.c:379-387, and MicWaitBusy, mic.c:244-252. They
  poll the lock word while it equals 1. The asm reads the labels gRtcLock
  and gMicLock, which are gRtcWork.lock (offset 0x0C) and gMicWork.lock
  (offset 0x04). C reads the struct field, the same word, with a volatile
  access.

Cross-checked against pokeplatinum-3ds patches/NitroSDK:

- 0006 (C versions): same function names. It disagrees with the HGSS asm
  in three places. This patch follows the asm.
  * GX_SendFifo48B and GX_SendFifo64B: 0006 stores every word to one
    address (*d = s[i]). The asm stores to pDest + 4 * (i % 3) and
    pDest + 4 * (i % 8). All of these are in the GXFIFO window
    (0x04000400-0x0400043F), so only the word left at each address after
    the send differs.
  * GXi_NopClearFifo128_: 0006 writes all 128 zeros to one address. The
    asm writes to reg + 4 * (i % 4).
  * OSi_WaitVCount0: 0006 stores 0 to IME. The asm stores HW_REG_BASE.
    Bit 0, the IME flag, is clear in both, so the interrupt state is the
    same. They differ only in the unused upper half of the 32-bit store
    at 0x0400020A. The asm's 32-bit accesses are kept.
- 0015 (lock-ID shift on 64-bit hosts): 0015 frees nothing when the
  offset is 32 or more. The ARM uses the bottom byte of the offset, so an
  ID whose offset has a low byte below 32 frees a bit. For example 0x160
  (offset 0x100) frees bit 31 of the second word on the DS. This patch
  follows the ARM. Valid IDs and OS_LOCK_ID_ERROR (0xFFFD, low byte 0x9D)
  behave the same as under 0015.
- 0024 (3D command ports): 0024 changes the callers in g3imm.c to
  NitroPort_GxDirectWrite, and leaves GX_SendFifo* alone. This patch does
  not touch g3imm.c. The FIFO sends here are plain stores, as in 0006. So
  matrix sends from HGSS's g3imm.c still do not reach the port's 3D
  translator until g3imm.c gets the 0024 treatment, in a separate patch.

Decisions:

- The FIFO sends and the NOP clear use plain stores, not
  NitroPort_GxFifoWords. g3imm.c stores the opcode as a plain store before
  the send. A packed-command decoder fed the matrix words without that
  opcode would run them as commands.
- NitroPort_Halt is declared locally, as in 0006. The survey include path
  does not reach 3ds_port/nitro/include.
- The guard is SDK_PORT_3DS, the pattern in the brief, not 0006's
  SDK_CW || __MWERKS__. The DS build never defines SDK_PORT_3DS.

Known limit: SDK_ARM7 with SDK_PORT_3DS does not compile. The C bodies
of OS_UnLockCartridge and OS_UnLockCard sit under the original
static inline (ARM7 only), which clashes with the header prototype.
The port builds no NitroSDK ARM7 code.

Checked: the survey (gcc, 64-bit and -m32) parses all eight files, up
from 147/190 and 152/190 files parsing before the patch to 155/190 and
160/190. The preprocessed text without SDK_PORT_3DS is identical to the
pinned tree for all eight files. tests/sdk/small/run.sh passes 54 of 54
cases.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/gx/g3x_nop_clear_fifo.c    | 13 +++++++
 src/gx/gxasm.c                 | 32 ++++++++++++++++
 src/mic.c                      |  9 +++++
 src/os/os_init.c               | 15 ++++++++
 src/os/os_spin_lock_id.c       | 68 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 src/os/os_terminate_proc.c     | 11 ++++++
 src/os/os_vram_exclusive_clz.c |  8 ++++
 src/rtc/rtc_api.c              |  9 +++++
 8 files changed, 165 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/gx/g3x_nop_clear_fifo.c b/src/gx/g3x_nop_clear_fifo.c
index 1cd67d2..2b7969b 100644
--- a/src/gx/g3x_nop_clear_fifo.c
+++ b/src/gx/g3x_nop_clear_fifo.c
@@ -6,6 +6,18 @@ void GXi_NopClearFifo128_(register void *reg);
 #include <nitro/code32.h>
 
 // clang-format off
+#ifdef SDK_PORT_3DS
+// C version of the asm below, for GCC. It stores 128 zero words in groups of four with stmia
+// to the same base (no writeback), so word i goes to reg + 4 * (i % 4). Plain stores.
+void GXi_NopClearFifo128_(void *reg) {
+    vu32 *dst = (vu32 *)reg;
+    int i;
+
+    for (i = 0; i < 128; i++) {
+        dst[i % 4] = 0;
+    }
+}
+#else
 asm void GXi_NopClearFifo128_(register void *reg) {
     mov r1, #0
     mov r2, #0
@@ -45,4 +57,5 @@ asm void GXi_NopClearFifo128_(register void *reg) {
     stmia r0, {r1, r2, r3, r12}
     bx lr
 }
+#endif
 // clang-format on
diff --git a/src/gx/gxasm.c b/src/gx/gxasm.c
index 84146cb..b9b0ea2 100644
--- a/src/gx/gxasm.c
+++ b/src/gx/gxasm.c
@@ -7,6 +7,22 @@ void GX_SendFifo64B(register const void *pSrc, register void *pDest);
 #include <nitro/code32.h>
 
 // clang-format off
+#ifdef SDK_PORT_3DS
+// C version of the asm below, for GCC. The asm reads 12 words and stores them in groups of
+// three with stmia to the same base (no writeback), so word i goes to pDest + 4 * (i % 3).
+// Those addresses are all in the GXFIFO window. Plain stores, as in Platinum's version: a
+// packed-command decoder must not see these words without their opcode, which the caller
+// stores as a plain store too.
+void GX_SendFifo48B(const void *pSrc, void *pDest) {
+    const u32 *src = (const u32 *)pSrc;
+    vu32 *dst = (vu32 *)pDest;
+    int i;
+
+    for (i = 0; i < 12; i++) {
+        dst[i % 3] = src[i];
+    }
+}
+#else
 asm void GX_SendFifo48B(register const void *pSrc, register void *pDest) {
     ldmia r0!, {r2, r3, r12}
     stmia r1, {r2, r3, r12}
@@ -18,9 +34,24 @@ asm void GX_SendFifo48B(register const void *pSrc, register void *pDest) {
     stmia r1, {r2, r3, r12}
     bx lr
 }
+#endif
 // clang-format on
 
 // clang-format off
+#ifdef SDK_PORT_3DS
+// C version of the asm below, for GCC. The asm reads 16 words and stores them in groups of
+// eight with stmia to the same base (no writeback), so word i goes to pDest + 4 * (i % 8).
+// Plain stores, as in GX_SendFifo48B.
+void GX_SendFifo64B(const void *pSrc, void *pDest) {
+    const u32 *src = (const u32 *)pSrc;
+    vu32 *dst = (vu32 *)pDest;
+    int i;
+
+    for (i = 0; i < 16; i++) {
+        dst[i % 8] = src[i];
+    }
+}
+#else
 asm void GX_SendFifo64B(register const void *pSrc, register void *pDest) {
     stmdb sp!, {r4, r5, r6, r7, r8}
     ldmia r0!, {r2, r3, r4, r5, r6, r7, r8, r12}
@@ -30,4 +61,5 @@ asm void GX_SendFifo64B(register const void *pSrc, register void *pDest) {
     ldmia sp!, {r4, r5, r6, r7, r8}
     bx lr
 }
+#endif
 // clang-format on
diff --git a/src/mic.c b/src/mic.c
index 3f8b8c6..2c4e321 100644
--- a/src/mic.c
+++ b/src/mic.c
@@ -241,6 +241,14 @@ void MicGetResultCallback(MICResult result, void *arg) {
 }
 
 // clang-format off
+#ifdef SDK_PORT_3DS
+// C version of the asm below, for GCC. Polls the same word: gMicLock is the label of
+// gMicWork.lock (offset 0x04 in MicWork), so the field is read directly.
+void MicWaitBusy(void) {
+    while (gMicWork.lock == 1) {
+    }
+}
+#else
 asm void MicWaitBusy(void) {
     ldr r12, =gMicLock
 @wait:
@@ -249,4 +257,5 @@ asm void MicWaitBusy(void) {
     beq @wait
     bx lr
 }
+#endif
 // clang-format on
diff --git a/src/os/os_init.c b/src/os/os_init.c
index f177e3b..83d0b9b 100644
--- a/src/os/os_init.c
+++ b/src/os/os_init.c
@@ -1,5 +1,19 @@
 #include <nitro.h>
 
+#ifdef SDK_PORT_3DS
+// C version of the asm below, for GCC. As the asm does, it saves IME as a 32-bit word,
+// stores HW_REG_BASE to IME (not 0; only bit 0 is defined, and it is clear), waits for
+// VCOUNT to reach 0 with a 16-bit read, and restores the saved IME word.
+void OSi_WaitVCount0(void) {
+    vu32 *ime = (vu32 *)REG_IME_ADDR;
+    u32 saved = *ime;
+
+    *ime = HW_REG_BASE;
+    while (reg_GX_VCOUNT != 0) {
+    }
+    *ime = saved;
+}
+#else
 asm void OSi_WaitVCount0(void) {
     mov r12, #HW_REG_BASE
     ldr r1, [r12, #REG_IME_OFFSET]
@@ -11,3 +25,4 @@ asm void OSi_WaitVCount0(void) {
     str r1, [r12, #REG_IME_OFFSET]
     bx lr
 }
+#endif
diff --git a/src/os/os_spin_lock_id.c b/src/os/os_spin_lock_id.c
index 2261135..3be546e 100644
--- a/src/os/os_spin_lock_id.c
+++ b/src/os/os_spin_lock_id.c
@@ -31,10 +31,17 @@ static inline void OSi_WaitByLoop(void) {
 
 #ifdef SDK_ARM7
 // clang-format off
+#ifdef SDK_PORT_3DS
+// C version of the asm below, for GCC: a tail call, so SVC_WaitByLoop gets the same count.
+void VENEER_SVC_WaitByLoop(s32 count) {
+    SVC_WaitByLoop(count);
+}
+#else
 asm void VENEER_SVC_WaitByLoop(register s32 count) {
     ldr ip, =SVC_WaitByLoop
     bx ip
 }
+#endif
 // clang-format on
 
 #endif
@@ -47,20 +54,34 @@ static inline
     // Nintendo decided they didn't want to use a define here,
     // so they made an asm func instead
     // clang-format off
+#ifdef SDK_PORT_3DS
+// C version of the asm below, for GCC: a tail call to OS_UnlockCartridge.
+s32 OS_UnLockCartridge(u16 lockID) {
+    return OS_UnlockCartridge(lockID);
+}
+#else
 asm s32 OS_UnLockCartridge(u16 lockID) {
     ldr r1, =OS_UnlockCartridge
     bx r1
 }
+#endif
 // clang-format on
 
 // For backwards compatibility.
 // Nintendo decided they didn't want to use a define here,
 // so they made an asm func instead
 // clang-format off
+#ifdef SDK_PORT_3DS
+// C version of the asm below, for GCC: a tail call to OS_UnlockCard.
+s32 OS_UnLockCard(u16 lockID) {
+    return OS_UnlockCard(lockID);
+}
+#else
 asm s32 OS_UnLockCard(u16 lockID) {
     ldr r1, =OS_UnlockCard
     bx r1
 }
+#endif
 // clang-format on
 
 BOOL OS_TryLockCard(u16 lockID) {
@@ -68,6 +89,31 @@ BOOL OS_TryLockCard(u16 lockID) {
 }
 
 // clang-format off
+#ifdef SDK_PORT_3DS
+// C version of the asm below, for GCC. Two words of free-ID bits: the first holds the IDs
+// from START, the second the IDs from START + 32. The highest set bit is the lowest free ID,
+// and taking it clears the bit. clz gives 32 for an empty word, so __builtin_clz is only
+// called on a non-zero word.
+s32 OS_GetLockID(void) {
+    vu32 *flag = (vu32 *)OSi_ANYP_LOCK_ID_FLAG;
+    u32 base = OSi_ANYP_LOCK_ID_START;
+    int word;
+
+    for (word = 0; word < 2; word++) {
+        u32 bits = *flag;
+
+        if (bits != 0) {
+            u32 n = (u32)__builtin_clz(bits);
+
+            *flag = bits & ~(0x80000000u >> n);
+            return (s32)(base + n);
+        }
+        flag++;
+        base += 32;
+    }
+    return OS_LOCK_ID_ERROR;
+}
+#else
 asm s32 OS_GetLockID(void) {
     ldr r3, =OSi_ANYP_LOCK_ID_FLAG;
     ldr r1, [r3]
@@ -119,9 +165,30 @@ _ex2:
     str r2, [r3]
     bx lr
 }
+#endif
 // clang-format on
 
 // clang-format off
+#ifdef SDK_PORT_3DS
+// C version of the asm below, for GCC. IDs from START + 32 up are in the second word. The
+// ARM shifts by the bottom byte of the offset, and a shift of 32 or more gives 0 (nothing is
+// freed). Same here, with the byte taken first, so C never shifts by 32 or more.
+void OS_ReleaseLockID(u16 lockID) {
+    vu32 *flag = (vu32 *)OSi_ANYP_LOCK_ID_FLAG;
+    u32 shift;
+
+    if (lockID >= OSi_ANYP_LOCK_ID_START + 32) {
+        flag++;
+        shift = (u32)lockID - (OSi_ANYP_LOCK_ID_START + 32);
+    } else {
+        shift = (u32)lockID - OSi_ANYP_LOCK_ID_START;
+    }
+    shift &= 0xFF;
+    if (shift < 32) {
+        *flag |= 0x80000000u >> shift;
+    }
+}
+#else
 asm void OS_ReleaseLockID(register u16 lockID) {
     ldr r3, =OSi_ANYP_LOCK_ID_FLAG
     cmp r0, #OSi_ANYP_LOCK_ID_START + 32
@@ -135,4 +202,5 @@ asm void OS_ReleaseLockID(register u16 lockID) {
     str r2, [r3]
     bx lr
 }
+#endif
 // clang-format on
diff --git a/src/os/os_terminate_proc.c b/src/os/os_terminate_proc.c
index 547697f..e173ebe 100644
--- a/src/os/os_terminate_proc.c
+++ b/src/os/os_terminate_proc.c
@@ -1,9 +1,20 @@
 #include <nitro.h>
 
 #ifdef SDK_ARM9
+#ifdef SDK_PORT_3DS
+// C version of the asm below, for GCC. The DS CPU sleeps until an interrupt (CP15 wait for
+// interrupt); the port decides what that means in NitroPort_Halt (3ds_port/nitro/src/
+// port_os.c). OS_Halt returns after it, as the DS does when the interrupt arrives.
+void NitroPort_Halt(void);
+
+void OS_Halt(void) {
+    NitroPort_Halt();
+}
+#else
 asm void OS_Halt(void) {
     mov r0, #0
     mcr p15, 0, r0, c7, c0, 4
     bx lr
 }
 #endif
+#endif
diff --git a/src/os/os_vram_exclusive_clz.c b/src/os/os_vram_exclusive_clz.c
index 9245a2d..f7f6d47 100644
--- a/src/os/os_vram_exclusive_clz.c
+++ b/src/os/os_vram_exclusive_clz.c
@@ -6,8 +6,16 @@ u32 OsCountZeroBits(register u32 bitmap);
 #include <nitro/code32.h>
 
 // clang-format off
+#ifdef SDK_PORT_3DS
+// C version of the asm below, for GCC. clz of 0 is 32 on the ARM; __builtin_clz(0) is
+// undefined in C, so 0 is handled here.
+u32 OsCountZeroBits(u32 bitmap) {
+    return bitmap ? (u32)__builtin_clz(bitmap) : 32;
+}
+#else
 asm u32 OsCountZeroBits(register u32 bitmap) {
     clz r0, r0
     bx lr
 }
+#endif
 // clang-format on
